1
00:00:01,040 --> 00:03:41,180
Part 10 stopped on the sentence of the railway station. This is the kind of mockery. If you go to a railway station, only pictures of women, and that bookstall, and they are selling only that story. So in this world it can be seen openly who wants to hear which subject. From this it came back to Srila Shukadeva Goswami. As men greedy for women hear talk of women, so you are taking a daily new taste in talk of Krishna. This is a wonderful comparison. It is an example. But it is completely true. And he says, this is the inborn nature of the saints. Of good people, of Krishna's devotees, the nature is like this. Nisarga means what is joined with birth itself. The practice that has been there from birth, or the nature that has become formed. Now no one makes an effort. As a man greedy for women does not take training anywhere in order to be attached to a woman. No one is taught that one should be attached like this, that one should talk like this. They stay attached by themselves. No one says, now start a week of this kind of story. Theirs keeps going. Unbroken. It is their nature. So this is the nature of devotees of the Lord like you. Because they take the essence. Those who bear the essence. In this world, what is the essence. The essence is talk of Krishna. The Lord is indeed the essence of the world. But in this world there are very many talks, very many books. The essence of all is Krishna-katha. So these take the essence. This is the inborn nature. For whom, for Krishna-katha alone, is the speech of the good. And their ear, and their mind. Speech, hearing, and mind for that purpose. All of theirs stays fixed in Krishna. Stays fixed in Krishna-katha. This is the nature of the good, that at every moment they keep making the katha of the infallible one new. They keep hearing. Fatigue never comes. They never get tired of it. As you are. The meaning of at every moment is at every word. As they hear, so the longing to hear keeps growing. This is the nature of devotees.

2
00:03:42,950 --> 00:08:59,630
Here one meaning is also this, that the speech also stays fixed in Krishna-katha alone. As talk of a woman is very pleasing to men greedy for women, in that way talk of the Lord is pleasing to the Lord's devotees. In this world there are only two subjects of talk that can stand against the Lord. Although in the world the Lord is an ocean of endless rasa. Before him, what attraction do women have. Nothing. But still, for the living beings bound by illusion, a woman is everything. And for the devotees, Krishna. For the good, Krishna. Between a woman and Krishna there is a kind of contest, who can attract more. Women are indeed victorious in the world. There is no doubt in this. Because the greater number is of men greedy for women. And the number of those greedy for Krishna is very small. The number is very great, so the name vita is being used in the plural, and woman in the singular. Very many men greedy for women keep talking of one woman. From this it is proved that for seeing one woman, lakhs of such men stay fixed. Talk of a woman, she sang this, this is the way. Now it is a thing of description from this platform, that the whole world is describing women alone. This thing that Shukadeva Goswami is speaking is in truth a completely true thing. There is a saying, to the lustful man a low woman is dear, and the earth to the miser. It is a very important saying of Shukadeva Goswami. And it is enough for understanding the glory of Maharaj Pariksit. The sight is happening, how attached Maharaj Pariksit is to Krishna, to Krishna-katha. Speech, hearing, and mind. To every human being the Lord has given this power. The power to hear, the power to speak, and the power to accept and reject, to remember. So devotees remember Krishna alone. Just as the greedy man is drawn to love of women, so Maharaj Pariksit. One acharya says, a question has been raised, why Srila Shukadeva Goswami is giving so crude an example with Maharaj Pariksit. Then they make the meaning with the help of one word. Because Krishna also is the supreme male, and with the higher nature. One meaning of the other man is the lover of another's wife. And the higher nature, that nature which is higher, is another's. This became one meaning. So the lila of the supreme male with the higher nature, their lila is happening, so there is a likeness with the vitas and with these men greedy for women. So he gave the example. It is not a wrong example. Maharaj Pariksit also is hearing his lila. The lila of the supreme male, with the higher nature also. They are hearing that same talk now.

3
00:09:01,300 --> 00:13:32,900
When people do a lila in this world, that is not called the higher nature. That is called the lower nature. But the Lord's lila of Vrindavan is fully spiritual. It is with the higher nature. And he is the supreme male. The best of all. Another meaning happened. Then, as some woman leaves her own husband and loves another man, and that other man loves that other woman, people in the world want very much to hear this matter. This has become the condition of people in the world. What is to be done. Love happened between the two. Then it is shown that both make the effort, let us meet, let our love remain. Like Laila and Majnun. They try. All these are false stories. They are not true. But they show them. And the writer is defeated. Society is defeated. And they make the effort to show them victorious. Why. Their relation is there, let them remain victorious. Mostly this same effort is made. We have not seen even one like this. But some stories have been read. They do as they please. People make this effort, that the relation which is unlawful should become victorious. Let society oppose, let the family oppose, they want to show that one victorious. I am not speaking a lie in this matter. Since people are corrupt. The mind is not right. So they want that. Then in this world people's taste is for hearing and telling matters of this kind. So the Lord himself has done this lila. Himself becoming the lover of another's wife, with his own eternal beloveds. He gave them birth in a different place. And then he did the early love with them. He met them. That is not a social relation. Society opposes. Still Krishna meets them. He shows the lila. So one purpose is here also, that the taste people have for reading a story of this kind, for hearing it, why should they not read my story. How I am meeting the wives of others, dancing, singing. And how they, leaving their husbands, love me. If one must stay, then let him read. Srila Prabhupada also writes this thing. And he also writes that some people have a great interest in politics. Then the Lord has played a great deal of politics for the throne of Hastinapura, and in other places also. So if this is to be heard, then hear Krishna's politics. If they want to hear that politics, then purification happens. The Lord is the lila of every kind of human being. Someone wants to stay in the line of propriety. Someone wants to serve society. In Sri Krishna's lila all of that is there. Because Sri Krishna himself is the Lord. The avatara of all. It is coming back to Srila Shukadeva Goswami, that Maharaj Pariksit's attachment in Krishna-katha is like the attachment these men greedy for women have for a woman.

4
00:13:36,640 --> 00:18:09,980
You are blessed. You have attachment in Krishna-katha. Then, having praised this much, he is beginning the katha again. The subject that was asked. Hear, having become careful, O king. I am telling you even the hidden thing. O king, you are looking very beautiful. You are seated in splendor. Because of attachment in Krishna-katha your beauty has increased. The meaning of king is this. O king. Hear with attention. Hear having become careful. Hear with the whole mind applied. This is a hidden matter. The event is in a great secret. Then, I am telling you. I am speaking to you. Because one principle is there, that the gurus tell even the hidden thing to the affectionate disciple. The gurus tell even the most hidden secret to their own loving disciple. Of the affectionate disciple. The meaning of affectionate is a disciple who has affection. Who does true love toward the guru, who does real love, he is called affectionate. In the age of now, disciples are such that however much opposition is in the mind, they do the guru's work. They do it even more than yesterday. They do it with the body also. But the number of those who oppose in the mind is greater. The gurus tell the hidden thing from the hidden. Here one thing should be kept in mind. One person cannot have only one guru. The word is gurus. It is said, gurus are many. For helping one living being, many gurus are needed. Someone teaches one subject. And that boy, having studied, one day becomes a fit person. In the same way the help of very many gurus is needed. In one scripture of respect, Lord Dattatreya has said this thing. From one guru, steady and complete knowledge does not come. Because Brahman, the Lord, is joined with endless variety. One person cannot describe all the variety of the Lord. Someone will tell one excellence of the Lord. Someone will tell another. In this way one person is walking on the path of Brahman, is walking on the path of the Lord, and many gurus help him. This should be learned. If a person in truth wants to advance on the path of the Lord, he needs the blessing of many people. As Suta Goswami. There also this word has come, the need of gurus. But yes, all the gurus should be tellers of one thing. This is very necessary. Not so that some guru says, this maha-mantra should be chanted, and someone says, no, another should be chanted. Then the guru is finished.

5
00:18:11,930 --> 00:22:48,800
Nowadays we have seen, somewhere a program happens, and many speakers are called onto one platform. And all, of different opinions, do not speak one thing. One says, he is without form. And the speakers have different intentions. Another says, you also are God. There is only the need to awaken the power. Once I was hearing. From the platform a person said, a tiger's cub. With birth itself, it was two or four days from birth, and it went into a herd of goats. It was a tiger's cub. It did not stay in the company of tigers. It went into the herd of goats. Then bleating like the goats, grazing grass. Whereas a tiger does not graze grass. But it was staying in the company of goats, so what could it do, it began to graze grass. And in the same way it became timid. In many ways it became a goat itself. In one way. But some tiger met it one day. He saw, the form and color are a tiger's. He began to roar. And from that he also made a breakfast of the goat. He was speaking like this. See, hold your own form. What are you. He was saying it openly to all. On the platform at Ayodhya. Some people had gathered in Ayodhya. And he was saying, by the distortion you are like a goat. You are a tiger, in truth. He was speaking in this way. And there was clapping. Then I was sitting there in one corner of ISKCON. I was watching. This is a cheating. The intention of my saying is that gurus can be many, but of one opinion. If the opinion has become different, then one guru alone is right. Then there is no need that there be many gurus. Yes, they are of one opinion, they are helping, on one path, one mantra, the same road, all is right, they are not changing, then it is right. There is no harm. Help should indeed be taken. As the nine yogendras had gone to Janakapura. Nine brothers spoke. Nine talks were given. And Maharaj Nimi asked them nine questions. Here it should not happen that one brother gives a talk that cuts another brother. All one. What is Bhagavata dharma. Who is called a Bhagavata. Then there are three kinds of Bhagavata. One who becomes a Bhagavata in this way, there, by the conduct of Bhagavata dharma, he crosses beyond illusion. Then the question came, what is illusion. Then illusion is the energy of the Lord. How the worship happens. These questions are being asked. And nine persons gave the talks. But all together they were one. It should be of this kind. Then a person who is telling a different opinion, satsang should not be done near him. Otherwise, on two boats. The gurus tell the hidden thing from the hidden to the affectionate disciple, to the loving disciple. So, Maharaj, hear carefully. It is a very hidden subject. He is beginning the answer to the question.

6
00:23:04,180 --> 00:29:00,890
On very beautiful sand of the bank. Having protected the calves and their keepers, the children, the Lord brought them to the sandbank of the Yamuna. Where above, very beautiful level sand was spread. Having brought them, having brought them back to life there. And then the Lord speaks. Ah, the sandbank is charming. O friends, O my companions, O my friends, how charming this sandbank is. Made full by our own play. Soft and good sand. Bloomed lotuses. The sound of bees. The sound of leaves. Crowded with trees. The Lord wants to eat. He wants to feed all. It had become very late. In the feeding itself it had become very late. Then they had gone into Aghasura's belly, that was a separate delay. But whatever articles the children had brought, for eating, even having gone into Aghasura's beak, all that food comes down just as it was. By the Lord's mercy. What has been written in the good act, the good acts we have done, and if later sins are also done, still the earlier good act that is with us is not destroyed. By the Lord's mercy. The children who brought food from home. This, made by the waves of the Yamuna, joined with very soft and good sand. It is sand, but it is not very large. Soft, good sand. Good means good. It is very good sand. It is soft. It is gentle. It is fit to sit on. And see, the bloomed fragrance of the lake. The lake that the Yamuna has become, here and there lotuses are bloomed in it. Bees are hovering on those lotuses. And in this forest, on all four sides, birds are singing. Their echo is happening. My friends, now all of you, you are agitated by hunger. The Lord, seeing the lotus faces of his friends wilted by hunger, is saying. Mercy has come. As mercy comes to a mother on seeing her child, that the child is hungry, in that way mercy is coming to the Lord, that they have become hungry. From a long time. Half the day. The day has climbed. The meaning of the day climbing is that two watches have passed. In the morning the children had gone, bringing food from home, and they had not eaten. Aghasura had eaten them. What had they eaten. The Lord says, here we should eat. Then the children accepted the vow. Because Krishna also was hungry. They had no attention to their own hunger. The children. They said, in order to feed Krishna, yes, yes, all right. And Krishna says, in order to feed them, the time to eat has come. Some children said, but the calves also should be fed. Before eating, the children used to give the calves water. Then the Lord says, the calves are nearby. Let these children be given water. Having drunk water, they will keep grazing nearby. Slowly, right here, they will keep grazing. Now the Lord had to have the calves stolen by Brahma. He says, the calves also, having drunk water right here, will keep grazing. There is no need to herd them. Let us receive the prasada, let us eat. And let these graze the grass. Then absorption came into the meal. Absorption came into the calves' eating also. They knew, we will graze very well, then Krishna will stay pleased. When the Lord sees the calves' bellies full, he becomes very happy. So, for Krishna's love.

7
00:29:01,150 --> 00:33:38,870
They sat behind, and the children sat on all four sides of them. Row after row. Many rows were set. They sat from all four sides. And Krishna's face was on every side. Every child was seeing this, that Krishna is sitting in front of me. Those who in fact were sitting behind, they also. They began to give the bite. The Lord manifested his opulence. For giving happiness to all the children. According to their taste. For eating his remnants. The Lord, having sat in this way. Those children who had brought prasada from their own homes. The beautiful limbs. They had not brought vessels from home. So, breaking a leaf from there, or in the bark of a tree, or on a leaf-plate. They do not spread a leaf-plate there, because it is the bank of the Yamuna, so there is no leaf-plate. Then what vessels were made, that description is coming. The children began to eat. First of all they would taste and see, how good the curd is, how good the rice is. Curd and rice they have brought mainly. And also some dishes, and some sweets also. From different homes they brought different things. Krishna had brought curd and rice. Then the other children, one who brought curd and rice, one who brought something, would first eat and see. And when it was very sweet, then they would say, Krishna, eat, eat, this is very sweet. Having eaten, then they would feed like this. Here, take this, eat this. And for feeding the children, when a great deal was served on the leaf, the Lord would say. They would serve. And they would give to others also. They would say, you eat, eat. They would eat it. Now no, now no. The Lord would say, that monkey is so clever. Look like this, a monkey. Then he would begin to look that way. Then the Lord, lifting his own, would fill it into that. You have not eaten anything yet. So in this way there was joking. Sometimes the Lord would snatch by force. Some, like Sridama, were narmas, the joking friends, who keep joking with Sri Krishna. Then, having eaten something, they would say, oh father, in my life I have never eaten something this beautiful. Then Krishna would say, give, give. Then he would run. I will not give, I will not give. Then the Lord, putting his own mouth into his mouth, would say, give, give. And he would give. In this way. Our acharyas have written this in the commentary. They would do it by force. In this way the Lord offers the food. He eats. And they would eat from Sri Krishna's mouth. And Sri Krishna would put from his own plate into someone's plate. There is purity of place, time, the vessel, and the thing. In how pure a way he is called. The Lord who enjoys the sacrifice. Come to the sacrifice, stay at the sacrifice, accept this. Here, take it. Drink it. With Vedic mantras the Lord is called. He is fed. And to see the love, Brahma stole the children. Let us see what Krishna does. How he searches, or weeps. For that. This is what Brahma wanted to see. No ignorance came to Brahma that this is the Lord. He knew fully that this is the Lord. He is God. Hare Krishna. Then the children said, all right.

8
00:33:38,990 --> 00:38:36,610
Then they gave the calves water. Having agreed, having given them to drink. Then however many calves there were, they took all of them to give water. Then they sat. And the Lord was in front of all. No child was seeing it so, that I am far from Krishna. Many rows were set. Row upon row. Every child was experiencing this, that I am sitting nearest to Krishna. This is a wonderful thing. What teaching the Lord gave here. Not the teaching of one who is liberated. And the food they had brought, which is called a packed meal. The meaning of a packed meal is to take it from home, to eat outside. Those who graze cows and buffaloes mostly eat like this. In the forest, outside, from home. And having opened it, they began to eat with the Lord. Its meaning is this, that all gave to Krishna. Krishna gave to all. All ate the prasada of all. It is not that one person is eating only his own. He is eating his own, it was not so. All brought. They ate together. They brought separately. They ate together. One should eat together. By eating together, love increases. For arguing like this, there are very many arguments. Then once it was said, one should eat together, love increases. Then one person said, some quarrel. On putting it all together they will eat with love. They will fight. But strange arguments are given. Logic has no standing. In truth, logic has no foundation. There is no basis. Anything can be said. The question itself had been made. I said, one should eat together. They began to eat, giving to one another. The meal together with the Lord. When the Lord lifted the morsel, then all began to eat. How they are sitting. That, Shukadeva Goswami says. On all sides of Krishna, many rows in a circle. On all four sides of Krishna. The meaning of on all sides is everywhere. Seated on all four sides of Krishna. A circle of many rows. The meaning of a row is a line. The meaning of many is many. Very many rows were set. You heard before, thousands. Then many rows will be set. But all were in front of Krishna. Facing him. They had turned their faces toward Krishna. Eyes bloomed. Their eyes were bloomed with joy. They have played with the Lord until now. They are eating with the Lord. This is bloomed eyes. A flower on the eyes. Then in that forest, in Vrindavan, how those seated children were shining. As the seed-pods of a lotus shine. The petals of a lotus stay on all four sides. And in the middle the saffron stays. In this way Sri Krishna is seated in the middle. And the children from all four sides. The comparison is being given with the bud of the lotus and the seed-pod of the lotus. Then the bud of a lotus, in it there is no difference of face, back, and the rest. In the same way, in Krishna there is no difference of face, back, and the rest. On every side it is face alone. On every side, the front. And the children were eating. They were feeding.

9
00:38:36,610 --> 00:43:29,980
It is a very large flower, and they joined it with a needle. As a lotus leaf is very large. It is of the flower. Then, separating the lotus leaf, spreading it, they placed the articles on it. Or they joined it. They sewed it with a needle. From one home no vessel had gone. The vessel for eating is separate. The one for washing the articles is separate. Then only enough for washing the articles was enough. How much to wash. They are small children. One should not go anywhere carrying a great net. The articles should be kept very few. And in front of all they keep eating, scattered. There is not even a special time for eating. But still, eating alone is the aim of life. Then what will they do. Eat, eat. The children brought from home. They did not bring articles for eating. They did not bring vessels. Then someone is eating on a flower. The meaning is an old leaf. And the meaning of a new shoot is a new leaf. Someone has a sprout. Some people ate in a sprout. They made the sprout a vessel. Here the meaning of sprout is, there are some plants whose sprouts come out broad. There is fruit. Some, the bark. There is the birch tree. On its bark, on the skin, they began to eat. Some brought a stone, broad, and began to eat on that. If the stone is smooth, then in truth it is better even than a plate. Let them eat on the stone. Having washed it, she keeps it again. Today they will have left it. Abundant prasada. Crows will come into it, or jackals will eat, and all will eat. They also need food. Far off, this feast was going. It was seated. And there was not even one vessel. Nowadays, suppose a hundred, two hundred, or a thousand people have gathered, and there is no leaf-plate, then what will they do. They will spread it on the rain. I saw it in one mahatma. Somewhere they were sitting. There was a place of cement like this. There was rain. Somewhere in this Braj the talk happened. Then people came. They gave prasada. Then there was a plate. But they brought something more, and there was no place for it. Then, taking it outside, they say, keep this. And above. The one of his also understood. Keep this. Later they would eat, lifting it from there. Later, having given two, she set it right. There is no need to increase a great necessity. Some people eat in the hand alone. They eat in the hand. They are called those whose vessel is the palm. Only as much as fitted in the hand, they will eat. Or they will cook by turns, then they will eat. With the same they drink water. The work of a glass, of a pot, of a plate, this joined palm does. The Lord has given human beings a hand such that it can become a vessel. For drinking water. For eating. For taking something. And in truth, for some sannyasi, for a sadhu, in what measure is there the right to eat. As much as the joined palms. And for a brahmachari, the joined palms alone are the vessel. And in one time, as much as happened, that much. Then, the one whose vessel is the palm. So those children were eating in all these things. Vessels made. Having made vessels from all these, those people were eating.

10
00:43:30,430 --> 00:47:20,030
Then, while eating, attention should be kept. Grave, simple, and some are joking friends. Like Madhumangala. The meaning of a joking friend is, joking means a joke. Whenever you look, some laughter with Krishna. Then even while eating, fountains of laughter were going. One should not laugh while eating. Another talk should not be done. But there, there is no grove of propriety. Even while eating, many were laughing. With the Lord, with God, they were all eating. Then they were showing each his own taste in food. The meaning of showing the taste in food is, having eaten, how good it is feeling. In this way. Ah, our articles are of the best class. So they were showing. Let Krishna ask. And it felt good to them also. So they would show the taste in food. They would praise. This spicy one, to me. Curd feels very good to me. Then Sri Krishna says, so give all the curd to this one. Then on this, laughter would happen now. What do you understand. Do you understand me as a glutton. What are you calling Madhumangala. Do you understand me as a glutton. You said the curd is good. Then its meaning is, I will eat all. They would say, the first right over food belongs to the brahmanas. Because the Lord made the brahmanas for eating. Krishna would say, blessed, blessed, eat, eat. So from their mouth, staying on their leaf, they would say, thirty-two twice-born are serving you. Thirty-two brahmanas are serving. Eat. Twice-born is also said of the tooth. A child's first tooth breaks. It takes birth a second time. So they also are called twice-born. The teeth, twice-born. The Lord would say, not one brahmana each, thirty-two brahmanas are serving. Eat. A joke of this kind was going. Then, laughing and making laugh. What were they eating. Even while eating, the play itself was going. Play while grazing the calves. Play while eating. Laughing, making laugh. No one was saying, it will spill. Do not make us laugh this much. What are you doing. Then in the laughing, curd and rice would also come sputtering out of Lord Krishna's mouth. Not here. Somewhere someone else was laughing. In this way. No propriety. No rule. Completely remnants. A full custom.

11
00:47:22,820 --> 00:55:24,330
Srila Shukadeva Goswami, singing, says. The enjoyer of the sacrifice. The Lord who enjoys the sacrifice is eating. Then see his form. While eating. Holding the flute between the belly and the cloth. They have tucked the flute into the cloth at the belly. They are eating. They are sitting like this. They are eating. Then they have tucked the flute here. The cloth at the belly. The cloth that is above the belly, the cloth, they have tucked it in that. Or, while sitting, the flute cannot be tucked, so they have kept it like this. Hanging it. One meaning of this has been made, that they have kept it between the belly and the cloth, both. Because any friend could have snatched it. And the cloth was the pouch. Only what they had worn. And when they are not playing, they keep it tucked in this. Here they are eating, so the hand has to be kept empty. So they have kept it here. Or they have tucked it. The flute. They have kept the flute like this. They call, taking the names of the calves. There is the sound of the horn. They call it the horn. They have tucked the horn. They have kept it in the left armpit. And the stick also in the other armpit. The meaning of the armpit became in both. Well, on one side they have kept the horn and the cane. In the left hand, a smooth morsel. And in the left hand, on his small palm, in the left hand, they have kept a smooth morsel. The meaning of smooth is kneaded. Ghee and curd. Ghee has been put into the curd. That already has ghee on it by itself. It is set curd. And the rice has been kneaded with it. The quantity of curd is more. Of rice, less. And it is completely solid. They have kept that. The morsel of curd and rice. Meaning, according to the finger, according to the hand, it is a vast ball. They have kept the morsel on the left hand. And the matching fruits on the fingers. The meaning of the matching fruits is the fruit fit for that curd and rice. Like a pickle of karira, or lemon, or chili. On the fingers. They are eating, then the pickle and the rest that has come, the Lord has kept on his own finger. The meaning of the matching fruit is what is fit for that food, fit for that morsel, which thing. These, with lemon. Pickle joined with lemon juice. Of ginger. Of chili. They have kept them. And of karira also. Then there is the pickle of karira. Of the caper. Then in that pickle, on its small fruits, its stem is attached. Then, holding the stem like this, it is hanging. Let him take it out. Having eaten like this, then they tuck it again. Then they are eating, and then they tuck it again. The morsel of curd and rice is in the left hand. And the pickle and the rest fit for that food, on those fingers alone. On the finger of the left hand alone. He himself is making them laugh. Making talk. Tell me, where the Lord makes a joke. When the Lord wants to make people laugh, how much talk he can speak that is fit for laughter. And he was making them laugh so the children would eat more. Having been made to laugh, it digests. Then they eat more. One should eat with happiness. One should not eat while weeping. Otherwise a person will stay very thin. Whatever food is received, the Lord's prasada, then, saying Nitai-Gaura-Hari a great deal, one should eat with joy. Hare Krishna, Hare Krishna, Krishna Krishna, Hare Hare. Hare Rama, Hare Rama, Rama Rama, Hare Hare. When it is eaten with joy, then the food also increases health. The Lord is eating. Its meaning is not that we should eat joking as the Lord jokes. On us that will not stay right. But still, one should eat with joy. Then the Lord also, the joking, telling joking stories of many kinds, was making them laugh. And he himself was also laughing. Heaven watching. All of heaven was present. In the sky. From heaven they were watching this sight. Eating, laughing. That same Lord who does not come in the sacrifice. A devotee once wrote, O Krishna, when you are called with the mantras of the sacrifice, you stay silent. You do not speak. And that same you call the calves and the cows saying hi hi. And with the small cowherd friends you joke this much. You speak. And the gopis abuse you. You bear that. An order was given to you. In childhood they would bring their own way. They would be equal. It came into someone's understanding, Krishna, you are under the control of love. You can be brought under control by love alone. Not by forced praises, by sacrifices. Then, if someone understands you as his own, loves you, then you answer the love. He understood. Then, the enjoyer of the sacrifice. He is watching. From very near. The gods themselves, like a cloud, all had climbed onto the airplanes. And they covered. Then they were watching, all clearly. In this way the Lord is eating. There was a very great absorption of the food, in truth. That absorption was not of the food. It was of eating with the Lord. Laughter, joking, all was going.

12
00:55:24,520 --> 00:58:29,000
And when the calves understood this, they are conscious calves, that Krishna and the cowherd friends are all eating, then they also fell to eating. A greed for grass came to them. Such was the Lord's lila. They also, grazing, hid in the inner forest. They went here and there in the forest. Those who were first in the field, who were being seen, now not even one calf was being seen. All went into the inner forest. The children were eating. Their soul, their mind, was fixed on the infallible one. Their attention did not go toward the calves. Suddenly, when the calves were not seen, someone's attention went. Then where did those calves go. All at once, the taste of the food, or the taste of the Lord's company. They were delighted. They were absorbed. Suddenly the children, the morsels they had taken as they had taken them, left the eating and drinking. They began to get up. Some began to get up. We are going, we are going. Where has our calf gone. All began to get up. Then the Lord said, stay seated. For searching. The Lord knew everything, what was going to happen. Those people had not gone into the inner forest at all. Now they had been stolen by Brahma. The Lord, holding the morsel of curd and rice at the belly, holding the pickle on the finger, holding the cane, is searching like this. He became just like one about to weep. He was defeated by searching. When they were not found, then he came here. He came here, and he saw that the children who were eating, the thousands, they also are not there. They began to think. They began to weep. What happened. And the all-knowing one knows all. But his lila energy, for a short time, is making him forget. Then they fell into a great confusion. Then he understood at once. Oh, this is my son's doing. This is Vidhi's doing. All right, he has stolen them. Then it is no harm. Om, to the Lord, the son of Vasudeva.

