00:58:54,350 --> 01:05:10,820
O descendant of Bharata, while the keepers of the calves were eating. Their selves absorbed. The calves, far into the inner forest. Made greedy by the grass. Krishna also, the fear. Friends, do not stop. I will bring the calves. O Pariksit of the line of Bharata. In this way, the keepers of the calves. While the keepers of the calves were eating. At the time of eating. Their selves on the infallible one. Whose mind was absorbed in Sri Krishna. The calves. But. In the inner forest. In the middle of the forest. Inside the forest. From far. Far. Far from that sandbank of the Yamuna. They entered. They went in. Made greedy by the grass. Having been made greedy by the green grass. So Sri Krishna is doing the eating lila with his own friends. Therefore the children's absorption happened in that play, in the childhood play, in the eating play. When in this world, having received ordinary food, and in an ordinary gathering, having received the articles of the whole group, people eat with this much joy. And they laugh, eat, and speak even at third-class things. Then where the things are very divine, and the Lord is sitting in the gathering, and he is making them laugh, he is laughing, then how much joy and absorption can be in their eating. Who can guess this. So those children were all sunk in supreme joy. They were eating. And everyone's mind was fixed on the infallible one. All were souls of the infallible one. The meaning of soul is sometimes the mind. Their mind was fixed on the infallible one alone. That infallible one himself had become their mind. The mind was so fixed on Krishna that it seemed the life-breath itself had gone into Krishna. That Krishna had gone into the life-breath. No difference is felt, whether Krishna is dwelling here or the life-breath is dwelling. Nothing is known. So those children had gone into Krishna. Their mind fixed on Krishna alone. Its meaning is, there was no attention to the calves. The work for which they had come from Braj into the forest, there was no attention toward that work. So when the minds of the Lord's friends were absorbed in this eating lila, with the Lord, at that same time, by the Lord's inconceivable yoga energy, this absorption was produced in the calves. They also became absorbed in grazing. They began to graze. And while grazing, they went very far from this gathering. Whereas this never used to happen. Those calves all wanted to stay near the Lord alone. But today, made greedy by the grass. On this, Srila Jiva Goswami writes that today it seems Brahma, having produced very beautiful grass, and making them greedy, took them far. Because he could not steal the calves in the path of the Lord's sight. Or in the path of any friend's sight. So, having produced greed by the grass, he took them. It was the greed for grass itself. The meaning of made greedy is that greed was produced in them. And this was the Lord's wish, in truth. In Braj, however many women there were who had sons, the mothers, in the mind of all this wish stayed, if Krishna would become our son, it would be very good. It was the wish of all. Even in the cows there was this wish, let Krishna become our son. So the all-knowing Lord, who is under love and feeling, kept thinking, how do I become the son of all. So today he wants to fulfill that. So the calves were removed. Far. Made greedy by the grass. And the children were eating. They were laughing. They were making laugh. All these lilas were going.

