01:05:10,820 --> 01:11:57,660
By then, suddenly, their attention went toward the calves. The calves were not there. Not seeing them, terrified by fear. Not seeing those calves, all the children became terrified by fear. What fear happened. The fear happened that somewhere they will jump into a ditch, they will fall, or they will drown in the Yamuna. Anything can happen. As disasters kept coming. As just now they had come, taken out of the python's belly. Somehow, by the Lord's mercy, by the mercy of the maintainer of the universe, they were saved. Then they. Fear happened. Having guessed the milk of the family. And the second fear happened, that mother and father will scold, that you people became so busy in eating that you do not graze the calves. This is one joy of a childhood lila, that the fear happened that they will scold, they will strike. They became terrified by fear. Suddenly this condition happened. First they were in the joy of the food. They were in the joy of the Lord's company. And all at once their face wilted. They fell into worry. They began to grieve. Then the Lord could not bear this pain of his own friends. Seeing them like this, he spoke. Even fear, of Krishna. How Krishna is. Of whom even fear. Of this universe also. From whom. The time by which this universe has fear, all living beings have fear, that fear also stays afraid of Sri Krishna. That same Lord is near these children, of whom even time is afraid. The time by which the whole world stays distressed, that time also fears the Lord. Then such a Lord, the giver of fearlessness to all, near those children. Now, with the word friends, the Lord is showing his natural affection. Toward the children. You are my friends. I do not want to see you unhappy. As you people are eating, eat. Do not stop. Do not leave the food. Eat. Then these people say, the calves have all gone. It is not known where they went. Then the Lord says, I will bring the calves here. You people know my power. Just now I killed Aghasura. Then I say, I am bringing them now. Then they say, they have not gone far. They are hidden in this bush right here. They are not far. If the Lord had said, they have gone far, I am going, then the children would all get up and go. We will go along. They do not leave Krishna alone. But he indicated so, that it is right here. You people eat. I am just bringing them. This feeling. And the Lord knows that those calves were stolen by Brahma. Or the lila energy at this time has bewildered the Lord. Sometimes the lila energy making him forget his omniscience, this also is an opulence of the Lord. This also is his being the Lord. It is wonderful. On this Srila Jiva Goswami has written a great deal. At great length. In our line, in giving this line the form of one principle, Jiva Goswami's hand is the greatest. He has arranged it from the Bhagavatam and from other books. Then he writes this thing at great length, why the Lord becomes forgetful in this way. Why in truth he is a child. The Lord in truth went in order to search. But there is so much affection for the children, so much affection, that he says, no, you people eat. The Lord does not want our devotees to be disturbed. You eat. We are going. How much love there is. Affection of the Lord. That he does not want to break that love of his own friends. That all at once they were in joy, and all at once, yes, searching while making them sad, they would be distressed. Then the food will stay lying just like this. Still a great deal remained to be eaten. Still the laughter was going. So the Lord says, from the food, do not stop. I will bring the calves. By the word I, the intention is that you people know my power. I am bringing them. The children all wanted, let us also go. You, Krishna, eat. We will go along. At the end of the chapter this thing came. The children did not eat even one morsel without Krishna. For one year. They stayed just like that. When the Lord came, that event happens after one year. Then they ate. I am bringing the calves.

