01:23:55,080 --> 01:31:14,450
Why did he steal. Someone else would have said, would have said to the Lord, you did not do right, this was done, that was done. Then what is the need of stealing the calves. Then Brahma thinks, by you the protection of the cows and the cowherds is indeed the work, O Lord of the Yadus. Brahma thinks in the mind, O Lord of the Yadus, your work is to protect the cowherds and the cows. But protecting their calves is my work. How. That you are the father. When you protect the cowherds and the cows, then I am your son. So my work is to protect the calves of the cowherds. Here, which work have you taken up. Ahead you will also protect the cows. And let us do the protection of their children, of the calves. So he lifted the children and took them. Because I will become their herdsman. I will graze the children. Perhaps Brahma has thought, we should be given one work. This is his own intention. I am your source. I am the son. Then when you graze the cows, grazing the sons of the cows is my right. Because I am your son. This is feeling natural. It should be. All right. Then why did he steal the children. On this they say, when Aghasura was freed from the bondage of the world, then Brahma began to think, what good act had this one done. Then he thought, the matter of his heart I do not know. The people who went inside his heart, those people will know. So perhaps he steals the children for this, that he will ask them, what good resolve was Aghasura making in the heart. When the children have come, having stayed in the heart, having stayed in his belly, they will know. They will have seen how much good thought is in his heart. What it is. Then Brahma's doubt will go. Perhaps for asking the children by turns. How he was liberated. They knew the divine glory of the Lord. But they wanted to see this charming glory. How Krishna is searching. And how he will expand himself in the form of cowherds and calves. This was the charming glory. Then this question. Why not. They could have scolded, why does he make a mistake like this. As they will scold Indra ahead. Or the gods. They used to scold. Then why are they not throwing Brahma down. Then they give its answer. One acharya says that the Lord did not forbid. Perhaps the Lord, thinking this, did not forbid. Whatever his wish is, let him do it. We ourselves become the calves. These will become the cowherd friends. To say this. He who was formerly established as Vidhi. How do I take him to the position of a prohibition. The one to whom I gave the post of Vidhi, how do I take him onto the word of a ban. So the Lord is searching. And Brahma stole the children. Then, not seeing the calves on the sandbank. When the Lord did not see the children, he became greatly distressed. Then, having tired, having come slow, he thought again, now the children will not be found. Then there was no vessel either. In the food, the basket, nothing. The food they had half eaten, all of that was not there. Brahma had taken everything. So the Lord, first, one search, where they were sitting. Were they sitting here, or were they sitting in another place. Then now he is searching for the children also. He is searching for the calves also. Both also. Krishna searched on every side. On every side. Every direction. Again. A second time, or three times, four times, five times, ten times. He is searching here. He is searching for the calves. The Lord is the knower of the universe. In the universe, where what is happening. What has happened. What will happen ahead. The Lord knows the matter of every second. But here he could not know where the calves are. Where they went. But at once, after this, he went ahead on this decision. That all was done by Vidhi. Vidhi has done all this. Of done by Vidhi, here there are two meanings. The Lord thought all. The arranger of all has done it. God has done it. But here the open meaning will be this, that Vidhi has done it. My son has done it. Krishna understood suddenly. Suddenly. He knew that Brahma stole them. The Lord did not go to ask anyone. It is not so that they put it in the newspaper and on television, where have the calves and the children gone, then it will be known. That also is not known. How many people are such that they put it out. They put out a pamphlet. They have it announced on the radio. And some relative of their house is lost. Missing. This sitting stops here.
